# {{ project_name }}

{{ project_description }}

Vertex AI Pipelines (KFP v2) project for **BigQuery ML** binary/multiclass **classification**,
with **Cloud Scheduler → Pub/Sub → Cloud Run** triggers and **Cloud Build** CI/CD.

## Pipelines

**Training:** ingest (BQ) → drift (PSI) → split → `CREATE MODEL` → `ML.EVALUATE` → metrics → Vertex Model Registry

**Prediction:** resolve model (registry → BQML id) → ingest → `ML.PREDICT` → summary

## Trigger path

```text
Cloud Scheduler (cron in terraform.tfvars)
        │
        ▼
   Pub/Sub topic (training | prediction)
        │  push + OIDC
        ▼
   Cloud Run  /pubsub/{kind}
        │
        ▼
   Vertex AI PipelineJob  (payload + KFP YAML from GCS)
```

## Setup

```bash
# requires Poetry: https://python-poetry.org/docs/#installation
make setup
# edit payload.json — project_id, tables, features, thresholds, service_account
# edit terraform/terraform.tfvars — crons, github_owner/repo, bucket
```

Prerequisites:

- [Poetry](https://python-poetry.org/) ≥ 1.8
- GCP project with Vertex AI, BigQuery, GCS, Pub/Sub, Cloud Run, Scheduler, Cloud Build APIs
- ADC or a service account with rights to apply Terraform and submit pipelines
- GitHub repo connected to Cloud Build (for triggers)

## Compile and run (local)

```bash
make compile
make trigger-training
make trigger-prediction
```

CLI equivalent:

```bash
poetry run python -m {{ package_name }}.trigger.submit training \
  --template artifacts/training_pipeline.yaml \
  --payload payload.json
```

## Infrastructure

Cron schedules live in [`terraform/terraform.tfvars`](terraform/terraform.tfvars):

```hcl
training_cron   = "{{ training_cron }}"
prediction_cron = "{{ prediction_cron }}"
```

```bash
make tf-init
make tf-plan
make tf-apply
```

After the first release image exists, set `trigger_image` in tfvars (or let Cloud Build update Cloud Run).

## CI/CD (Cloud Build)

| Trigger | When | Config |
|---------|------|--------|
| PR | PR → `main` | [`cloudbuild/pr.yaml`](cloudbuild/pr.yaml) — Poetry install, pre-commit, unit tests, KFP compile |
| Push | push → `main` | [`cloudbuild/push.yaml`](cloudbuild/push.yaml) — `terraform apply` |
| Release | tag `vX.Y.Z` | [`cloudbuild/release.yaml`](cloudbuild/release.yaml) — docker build/push, copy KFP artifacts to GCS, deploy Cloud Run, optional e2e |

Connect the GitHub app / Cloud Build repository, set `github_owner` + `github_repo` in tfvars, then `make tf-apply`.

## payload.json

| Key | Purpose |
|-----|---------|
| `project_id` / `region` | GCP project and Vertex location |
| `pipeline_root` | GCS URI for pipeline artifacts |
| `service_account` | Optional SA email for `PipelineJob.submit` |
| `source_table` / `baseline_table` | Training + drift baseline tables |
| `feature_columns` / `label_column` | Model schema |
| `model_type` | `LOGISTIC_REG` or `BOOSTED_TREE_CLASSIFIER` |
| `drift_psi_threshold` / `min_roc_auc` | Quality gates |
| `model_resource_name` | Optional Vertex model id for prediction (else display name lookup) |

## Layout

```text
src/{{ package_name }}/
  components/   # KFP @component ops
  pipelines/    # training + prediction DSL
  trigger/      # aiplatform.PipelineJob submitter
  service/      # Cloud Run FastAPI (Pub/Sub push)
terraform/      # Pub/Sub, Cloud Run, Scheduler, Cloud Build triggers
cloudbuild/     # pr / push / release configs
payload.json
Dockerfile
pyproject.toml   # Poetry
Makefile
```
